<section class="section-cs"><div class="container-cs"><div class="row-split-cs"><div class="overline-pd">The challenge</div><div class="col-main-cs"><h2 class="h3-text-cs">Two very different audiences, several apps and a website that no longer felt like one product.</h2><p class="body-cs">Bohemian Research runs a global research panel. Millions of people across 80+ countries and 32 languages answer surveys, and agencies, universities and brands use that panel to reach respondents. Panel members want apps that feel rewarding and easy to use. Researchers want a partner they can trust with their data and their deadlines.</p><p class="body-cs">The company had grown fast and launched games, and the old setup served neither side well. The brand felt serious but flat. Each app lived in its own world. The website spoke to everyone at once: the headline described a category instead of a service, the strongest proof sat halfway down the page, and visitors had several competing things to click.</p></div></div></div></section>
<section class="section-cs"><div class="container-cs"><div class="overline-pd">Apps</div><h2 class="h2-cs">Three apps that feel like one family</h2></div><div class="gallery-cs"><div class="row-2-cs"><img src="/case-studies/bohemian/a1.webp" loading="lazy" alt="Street ad for the Multipolls app with the line Your opinion pays" class="tile-ar-cs" style="--ar:625/798"/><img src="/case-studies/bohemian/a2.webp" loading="lazy" alt="Games screen in the Multipolls app" class="tile-ar-cs" style="--ar:625/798"/></div><img src="/case-studies/bohemian/a3.webp" loading="lazy" alt="Three Multipolls screens: invite friends, balance overview and play games to earn money" class="tile-ar-cs is-wide-cs is-phones-boh-cs" style="--ar:1274/757"/><div class="row-2-cs"><img src="/case-studies/bohemian/a4.webp" loading="lazy" alt="Cashout screen with gift cards from well-known brands" class="tile-ar-cs" style="--ar:625/798"/><img src="/case-studies/bohemian/a5.webp" loading="lazy" alt="Game detail with the rewards a player can unlock" class="tile-ar-cs" style="--ar:625/798"/></div><div class="caption-cs">Multipolls, the flagship app: invite friends, the balance overview, games and cashing out</div></div></section>
<section class="section-cs"><div class="container-cs"><div class="row-split-cs"><div class="overline-pd">Brand identity</div><div class="col-main-cs"><h2 class="h3-text-cs">Playful, but confident.</h2><p class="body-cs">Once Bohemian Research launched games, the brand had to become more playful. The risk was going too far and losing the credibility researchers need before they hand over a project.</p><p class="body-cs">Bold shapes and colour bring energy to the apps and the games, while a clean layout and clear typography keep the website calm and trustworthy. The same identity now runs across the website, the apps and the marketing materials, which is what makes the panel feel like a single product instead of a collection of them.</p></div></div></div></section>
<section class="section-before-dark-cs"><div class="gallery-cs"><img src="/case-studies/bohemian/b1.webp" loading="lazy" alt="Poster campaign for Bohemian Research on a city street: Your opinion pays" class="tile-ar-cs is-wide-cs" style="--ar:1274/717"/><div class="row-2-cs"><img src="/case-studies/bohemian/b2.webp" loading="lazy" alt="Golden Surveys onboarding screen" class="tile-ar-cs" style="--ar:625/798"/><img src="/case-studies/bohemian/b3.webp" loading="lazy" alt="Golden Surveys spin-the-wheel reward after a completed survey" class="tile-ar-cs" style="--ar:625/798"/></div><div class="caption-cs">The brand in the real world, and Golden Surveys: onboarding and the spin-the-wheel reward after a completed survey</div></div></section>
<section data-nav="dark" class="section-video-cs section-monitor-boh-cs"><div class="container-cs"><div class="overline-pd lime-pd">Website</div><h2 class="h2-video-cs">Got a survey? <span class="span-line-cs">We&#x27;ll get you respondents.</span></h2><p class="body-cs body-dark-boh-cs">The old headline was &quot;The end-to-end market research solution&quot;. Same company, but now the page says what it does in one line. The redesigned site is built in Framer, and every change followed one question: what does a researcher need to see to decide quickly?</p></div><img src="/case-studies/bohemian/monitor.webp" loading="lazy" alt="The redesigned Bohemian Research homepage on a desktop display" class="img-monitor-boh-cs"/></section>
<section class="section-after-dark-cs"><div class="gallery-cs"><img src="/case-studies/bohemian/w1.webp" loading="lazy" alt="The redesigned homepage: hero, client logos and the key numbers" class="tile-ar-cs is-wide-cs is-home-boh-cs" style="--ar:1280/960"/><img src="/case-studies/bohemian/w2.webp" loading="lazy" alt="Rewards section with gift cards from well-known brands" class="tile-ar-cs is-wide-cs" style="--ar:1280/720"/><img src="/case-studies/bohemian/w3.webp" loading="lazy" alt="Product visuals for researchers: survey insights and audience quality" class="tile-ar-cs is-wide-cs is-pair-boh-cs" style="--ar:1280/552"/><img src="/case-studies/bohemian/w4.webp" loading="lazy" alt="Closing call to action with one Request demo button" class="tile-ar-cs is-wide-cs" style="--ar:1280/720"/><div class="caption-cs">One page for everyone became three clear paths, the proof moved to the first screen, and a few different buttons became one: Request demo</div></div></section>
<section class="section-cs"><div class="container-cs"><div class="overline-pd">For researchers</div><h2 class="h2-cs">What a researcher gets, shown instead of described</h2></div><div class="gallery-cs"><img src="/case-studies/bohemian/p1.webp" loading="lazy" alt="Pricing and CPI control next to an offerwall position preview" class="tile-ar-cs is-wide-cs" style="--ar:1274/705"/><div class="row-2c-boh-cs"><img src="/case-studies/bohemian/p2.webp" loading="lazy" alt="Estimated completion and incidence rate on a chart" class="tile-ar-cs" style="--ar:698/552"/><img src="/case-studies/bohemian/p3.webp" loading="lazy" alt="Audience targeting by age range, gender and country" class="tile-ar-cs" style="--ar:552/552"/></div><img src="/case-studies/bohemian/p4.webp" loading="lazy" alt="Call to action: get access to unique audiences" class="tile-ar-cs is-wide-cs" style="--ar:1274/717"/><div class="caption-cs">Pricing, timing and audience shown as small product visuals, so the page says plainly how fast a survey goes live</div></div></section>
<section class="section-cs"><div class="container-cs"><div class="row-results-cs"><div class="col-results-cs"><div class="overline-pd">Result</div><h2 class="h2-results-cs">Conversions went up 23% after the new website launched.</h2><p class="body-results-cs">The brand, the website and the apps now work as one system. A visitor who lands on the website recognises the same company inside every app.</p><p class="body-results-cs">On the website the apps are presented together as one panel: more apps and more ways to earn for members, and a bigger panel for researchers.</p><div class="faq-cs"><h3 class="faq-cs-h">Questions about this project</h3><details class="cell-questions faq-cs-item"><summary class="faq-cs-q"><div class="title-large">What did rh.design do for Bohemian Research?</div><span class="faq-cs-plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><p class="desctiption faq-cs-a">A new brand identity, a redesigned marketing website built in Framer, and the design of all three apps: Multipolls, RewardsRoo and Golden Surveys.</p></details><details class="cell-questions faq-cs-item"><summary class="faq-cs-q"><div class="title-large">What changed on the website?</div><span class="faq-cs-plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><p class="desctiption faq-cs-a">The homepage now says what the company does in one line: “Got a survey? We’ll get you respondents.” The proof, users, countries and languages, moved to the first screen, and several buttons became one: Request demo.</p></details><details class="cell-questions faq-cs-item"><summary class="faq-cs-q"><div class="title-large">How do three apps stay one brand?</div><span class="faq-cs-plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><p class="desctiption faq-cs-a">They share one design system. Bold shapes and colour give the apps and games their energy, and the same identity runs across the website, the apps and the marketing materials.</p></details><details class="cell-questions faq-cs-item"><summary class="faq-cs-q"><div class="title-large">What was the result?</div><span class="faq-cs-plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><p class="desctiption faq-cs-a">Website conversions went up 23% after the new site launched. The panel now reads as one product across 80+ countries and 32 languages.</p></details></div></div><div class="stats-col-cs"><div class="stat-row-cs"><div class="stat-big-cs">+23%</div><div class="stat-label-cs">Website conversions</div></div><div class="stat-row-cs"><div class="stat-big-cs">3</div><div class="stat-label-cs">Apps in one design system</div></div><div class="stat-row-cs"><div class="stat-big-cs">80+</div><div class="stat-label-cs">Countries in the panel</div></div></div></div></div></section>
